Skin Creator 3D — Privacy Policy

Last updated: November 10, 2026

Thank you for using Skin Creator 3D (the "App"), a skin and character editor for iPhone and iPad. Your privacy is important. This Privacy Policy explains, in plain language, what data the App handles and what it does not.


Developer

Skin Creator 3D is developed by Dzianis Milasheuski, an individual developer based in Lithuania. For any questions about this policy or the App, contact: info@porconova.com


Summary

Skin Creator 3D runs on your device. The only time it contacts the internet on its own is when you ask it to look up a Minecraft: Java Edition player's public skin by name (see below). The developer operates no servers, has no account system, and does not collect any data about you or about how you use the App — no analytics, no tracking, no advertising. Your characters, skins, looks, and settings stay either on your device or in your personal iCloud account, never on the developer's infrastructure.


What the App Does Not Collect

•  The App has no sign-up, no login, no user account.
•  The App does not collect or transmit your name, email, phone number, contacts, location, photos, or files to the developer or to anyone else. The one exception you control is a player name you type for a Java skin lookup, which goes to Mojang as described below.
•  The App does not collect usage statistics, analytics, crash reports of its own, or any device identifiers.
•  The App does not contain advertising SDKs, analytics SDKs, social-network SDKs, or cross-app tracking SDKs.
•  The App does not use cookies or advertising identifiers (IDFA).
•  The App does not sell, share, rent, or disclose user data to third parties.


Data That Stays on Your Device

The following information is created by you and stored locally inside the App. It is not transmitted to the developer:

•  Your characters: their skins, looks (outfit variants), layers, base mask, names, and arm model (Classic or Slim).
•  Version history snapshots of your characters and the "Recently deleted" list, which is cleared automatically after 30 days.
•  App preferences (for example, which tips you have already seen).

Reference pictures you add while painting are kept only while the character is open and are not saved.


iCloud Drive (optional)

If you turn on "Sync with iCloud" in the App's Settings, your characters and their version history are stored in the App's private folder in your personal iCloud Drive so they can sync to your other devices signed in to the same Apple Account. This storage is provided by Apple under Apple's terms. The developer has no access to your iCloud data. You can turn sync off at any time; your characters are then kept on the device.


Photos and Files

•  Importing: when you choose "Import from Photos" or "From Files", the system picker shows your library and only the single picture or file you select is handed to the App. The App does not get access to the rest of your photo library.
•  Saving: when you choose "Save Image" in the share sheet, iOS asks for permission to add images to your photo library. The App can only add images you export; it cannot read your library.


Sharing and Exports

When you export or send something — a skin PNG, a picture or GIF of a pose, a Minecraft skin pack (.mcpack), or a character file (.skincreator) — the file is created on your device and goes only where you choose to send it (for example Minecraft, Files, AirDrop, or Messages). The developer does not receive a copy. A .skincreator character file contains the character's skins, looks, and name; share it only with people you want to have them.


Java Player Skin Lookup (optional)

In Mix & Match you can take parts from the public skin of a Minecraft: Java Edition player by typing that player's name and tapping "Find". Only then, the App sends the name you typed to Mojang's public services (api.mojang.com and sessionserver.mojang.com), which return the player's ID and skin address, and then downloads the skin picture from textures.minecraft.net. As with any internet request, Mojang's servers also see your IP address. These services are operated by Mojang / Microsoft under their own privacy policy (https://privacy.microsoft.com). The request is made without cookies or a stored cache, the name is not saved by the App, and nothing is sent to the developer. If you never use this lookup, the App makes no such request.


Purchases (Apple App Store)

Skin Creator 3D offers optional purchases through Apple's In-App Purchase system: the Skin Creator Pro+ subscription (monthly or yearly), a one-time Pro Forever purchase, and outfit packs. All payments are processed by Apple. The developer never receives your name, payment method, billing address, or any other financial information. Apple's StoreKit framework only tells the App which purchases are active on your Apple Account, so the App can unlock the matching features.

You can manage or cancel an active subscription in Settings → [Your Name] → Subscriptions on your device.


Children

The App does not collect personal information from anyone, including children. Purchases are made through Apple and are subject to Apple's parental controls, such as Family Sharing and Ask to Buy.


Your Rights

Because the App does not collect personal information on the developer's side, there is no developer-held data for you to access, correct, export, or delete.

•  Data stored on your device can be removed by deleting individual characters inside the App (and then from "Recently deleted"), or by deleting the App.
•  Data stored in your iCloud Drive can be removed by turning off iCloud for the App or by deleting it from your iCloud storage in iOS Settings.
•  An active subscription can be cancelled in your Apple Account subscriptions; this is governed by Apple's terms and the developer cannot cancel it for you.


Regulatory Notes

The App is designed so that no personal data is collected by the developer or by any third party on the developer's behalf. Under the EU GDPR and the California CCPA / CPRA, the developer therefore does not act as a controller or processor of your personal data in connection with the App. Where Apple provides purchases and iCloud storage, those activities are governed by Apple's own privacy policy. The optional Java player skin lookup is a request you send directly to Mojang and is governed by the Microsoft privacy policy.


Trademarks

Skin Creator 3D is not an official Minecraft product. It is not approved by or associated with Mojang or Microsoft. "Minecraft" is a trademark of Mojang Synergies AB.


